 ```ts
 resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
 ```
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Patch, as [RFC 6902](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902),
+to a JSON document. The patch is an array of the six operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`;
+the operations are applied in order, each to the result of the previous one.
+
+It returns the changed document as a new value and never modifies its inputs, so a caller can keep the original
+document, for example to compare it with the result or to retry. It throws a `JsonPatchError` when the patch is malformed
+or when an operation fails, for example a missing member, an index out of range, or a `test` whose value differs.
+The whole patch is checked for shape before any operation runs. When the failure comes from a malformed JSON Pointer,
+the error's `cause` is the `JsonPointerError`.
+
+```ts
+applyPatch({ foo: ["bar"] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/foo/-", value: "baz" },
+  { op: "test", path: "/foo/0", value: "bar" },
+]); // { foo: ["bar", "baz"] }
+```
